[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 500,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 539,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71382,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 539,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Extranodal marginal zone lymphoma of mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue (MALT lymphoma) is an extranodal lymphoma composed of marginal zone B&nbsp;cells (centrocyte-like cells), cells resembling monocytoid cells, small lymphocytes, large lymphoid cells resembling centroblasts or immunoblasts, and plasmacytic cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 501,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 540,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71383,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 540,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9699/3 Extranodal marginal zone lymphoma of mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 502,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 541,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71384,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 541,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A85.3 &amp; XH3FE9 Extranodal marginal zone B-cell lymphoma, primary site excluding stomach or skin &amp; Mature B-cell lymphomas</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 503,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 542,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71385,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 542,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 504,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 543,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71386,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 543,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 505,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 544,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71387,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 544,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MALT lymphoma may occur at any location in the genitourinary tract; the urinary bladder is the most common site {9351570; 19377442; 32664075}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71388,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The presenting symptoms are location-dependent and may include haematuria, frequency, urinary obstruction, dysuria, and lower abdominal pain {9351570; 19377442}. Some patients are asymptomatic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71389,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MALT lymphoma is the most common primary low-grade lymphoma involving the genitourinary tract {9351570; 19377442; 29187485}. MALT lymphoma of the genitourinary tract accounts for &lt;&nbsp;5% of extranodal lymphomas and &lt;&nbsp;1% of all genitourinary tumours. There is a slight female predominance {29187485}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71390,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Because there is no native lymphoid tissue in the mucosa of the genitourinary tract, the lymphoma arises from lymphoid tissue acquired as a result of a chronic inflammatory process or an immunological disorder (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20877\" target=\"_blank\">#20877</a>Table&nbsp;11.02) {32664075; 11821481; 22297664; 31825109}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71391,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Chromosomal translocations associated with MALT lymphomas have been rarely reported (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20877\" target=\"_blank\">#20877</a>Table&nbsp;11.02) {23690413; 17709321; 12101213}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71392,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>MALT lymphomas may appear as single or multiple masses that are pale pink or tan in colour and firm, solid, or fleshy, with overlying distended vessels, erythema, and focal necrosis {10911804; 16390244; 18184182; 32664075; 30511263}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71393,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histology is characterized by a diffuse infiltrate of centrocyte-like cells with moderate amounts of pale-staining cytoplasm accompanied by scattered larger nucleolated cells and cells showing plasmacytic features. Lymphoepithelial lesions are not frequent. Residual reactive follicles with or without follicular colonization by lymphoma cells may be seen. Rare cases show amyloid deposition. Ki-67 expression is usually low (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20878\" target=\"_blank\">#20878</a>Table&nbsp;11.03, and <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20879\" target=\"_blank\">#20879</a>Table&nbsp;11.04) {11378561; 11385310; 17709321}. Rare cases may show transformation to diffuse large B-cell lymphoma {25837971}. Ki-67 immunostaining can be a good aid for this assessment {17709321}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71394,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>On urine cytology, MALT lymphoma is characterized by dispersed, single, atypical, small to medium-sized lymphoid cells with a high N:C&nbsp;ratio and hyperchromatic nuclei without nucleoli, and it can mimic urothelial carcinoma {23078009}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71395,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Molecular pathology is not essential for the diagnosis (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20877\" target=\"_blank\">#20877</a>Table&nbsp;11.02).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71396,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20879\" target=\"_blank\">#20879</a>Table&nbsp;11.04 .</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/36/275/20879\" target=\"_blank\">#20879</a>Table&nbsp;11.04 ; in addition: demonstration of light chain restriction; demonstration of follicular dendritic cell meshworks using CD21 and/or CD23 immunohistochemistry; low Ki-67 proliferation index.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 552,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71397,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 552,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The Lugano classification is used for staging extranodal marginal zone lymphoma. The Ann Arbor staging system has often been used for non-gastric extranodal marginal zone lymphoma {31912792; 26773441}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 514,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 553,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 71398,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 275,
        "headingId": 553,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is important to assess for large nucleolated cells in sheets or in a high proportion (&gt;&nbsp;20%) to exclude progression to diffuse large B-cell lymphoma.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-25T16:57:06"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]